<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Is North Korea holding back on sending Russia more troops?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c42af5f74d62e10104cc3e99c7030b6e07fbcdcd577aeb2a6ad2b833f1911848</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:55:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T12:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-north-korea-holding-back-on-sending-russia-more-troops/a-80033025--db490ffc00f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-north-korea-holding-back-on-sending-russia-more-troops/a-80033025?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A North Korean troop buildup Ukraine warned about months ago has yet to materialize, even as strategic cooperation continues. Analysts say Pyongyang is balancing its ties with Moscow and Beijing.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU imposes import quotas for hybrid vehicles from China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8077577be7c0c394ff2a2912bc666db7a62cec8966510d381a49a9122d838a4</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:56:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T10:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-imposes-import-quotas-for-hybrid-vehicles-from-china/a-80029981--7d148967ab4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-imposes-import-quotas-for-hybrid-vehicles-from-china/a-80029981?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU is trying to protect its own car manufacturers from what it called "overcapacity" in China. Carmakers in the bloc, especially in Germany, have been lagging behind their Chinese rivals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistani astronaut to join Chinese space mission</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b3c6fe47aa48eb93eb70d23f1bc315c9ef07bc9e8fbd77a935b993d5192fefc</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistani-astronaut-to-join-chinese-space-mission/a-80028922--3c985eac77fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistani-astronaut-to-join-chinese-space-mission/a-80028922?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Pakistani astronaut is set to become to the first foreigner to board China's Tiangong space station. Muhammad Zeeshan Ali, a payload specialist, will join the Shenzhou-24 mission when it launches on Wednesday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Chinese official gets death sentence in spy case, report says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac0cf8e5360db76f06a202c99f9e3bf22db06d3abd4dee8ad65ee4b94c607dbd</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T08:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/chinese-official-gets-death-sentence-in-spy-case-report-says/a-80028393--388878bff1dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/chinese-official-gets-death-sentence-in-spy-case-report-says/a-80028393?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Chinese official recruited while working abroad was paid more than a million yuan to leak secrets, state-affiliated media reported.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Exiled leader Sheikh Hasina plans to return to Bangladesh on Dec. 16</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:faa2e990965153f7cb7cdef56a762391086e600fdfc3a5f479c4423badb2fe9f</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T07:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/exiled-leader-sheikh-hasina-plans-to-return-to-bangladesh-on-dec-16/a-80028083--b9b8951e810c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/exiled-leader-sheikh-hasina-plans-to-return-to-bangladesh-on-dec-16/a-80028083?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two years of exile in India, ousted Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina has set a return date to Bangladesh. She was sentenced to death in absentia last year over a brutal crackdown that left hundreds dead.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India: Report warns of deepening authoritarianism under Modi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d939f987ebb25d64b168ce2be122e65c9023e157565088b6c155c16a090b93cd</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-report-warns-of-deepening-authoritarianism-under-modi/live-80027405--62ea9ba89a08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-report-warns-of-deepening-authoritarianism-under-modi/live-80027405?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Human Rights Watch report found that Modi's rule in India has eroded the rule of law and "systematically weakened institutions" meant to protect freedoms. Also, in Delhi a man injured nine police with a knife.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US adds Megaspeed, at center of Nvidia scandal, to a trade blacklist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:360e40ce32c49f2ca25a0822cf350769652686877402b53ff968c1e70fd5b801</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T22:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-adds-megaspeed-at-center-of-nvidia-scandal-to-a-trade-blacklist/a-80026849--f5370c0bb019.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-adds-megaspeed-at-center-of-nvidia-scandal-to-a-trade-blacklist/a-80026849?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration has added Megaspeed to a trade blacklist after tensions over its failure to do so raised questions. The news came the same day that Jensen Huang was reinstated as Nvidia's CEO.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After Japan's APEC snub, what's next for its China ties?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0cb43eb42af3c74347cd814f359b0bda446fc109fb0b35fd9cf43eb600ac0b6f</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-japan-s-apec-snub-what-s-next-for-its-china-ties/a-80020823--0940c063c8fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-japan-s-apec-snub-what-s-next-for-its-china-ties/a-80020823?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan has long-running concerns over Chinese military expansionism, and Beijing has bristled at Sanae Takaichi's comments on Taiwan. The frosty ties were on full display at the APEC summit.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gukesh to defend chess crown against rising star Sindarov</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ed9c9702cfecbb22928fd12d689b5046f212483b9eadef16d263a46d989b815</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806--07e5204aa07f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the World Chess championship gets underway, it's no coincidence that the titleholder, Gukesh Dommaraju, and his challenger, Jakhovir Sindarov, are both from Asia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal's new PM eyes closer ties with India amid lingering disputes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbe211b9253ff67a4328674aaf8e236e15f44463b7277752cc95f64c91acc248</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-new-pm-eyes-closer-ties-with-india-amid-lingering-disputes/a-80021769--65c0c20879de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-new-pm-eyes-closer-ties-with-india-amid-lingering-disputes/a-80021769?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On his first foreign bilateral visit, rapper-turned-Prime Minister Balendra Shah sought deeper ties with Nepal's neighbor and largest trading partner, while steering clear of sticky territorial issues.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA presidential election 2027: Infantino facing Diallo and Tashima — could an alliance change everything?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5d9b6125e17cd56fed8a63c7ad246e37603a64e80263920b52a1073cd3a2152</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everyth/a-80002882--01040a665cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everything/a-80002882?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two challengers to Gianni Infantino have registered for next year's FIFA presidential election. What do Philippe Diallo and Kozo Tashima stand for – and do they stand a chance against the incumbent?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan minister to visit India, but no breakthrough expected</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbad263e975361b7896f254012d1320aaf7ca81c01983c492315e060ecb5ce60</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717--07503556e8b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-minister-to-visit-india-but-no-breakthrough-expected/a-79991717?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Pakistani minister's visit to India for a Shanghai Cooperation Organization forum marks a rare high-level contact between the two archrivals, but analysts say it does not signal a resumption of bilateral engagement.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's growing exodus of young talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04fc1230a9b4b6eccf5b28998471636109e173b8673d5ef0e25549390734ac5f</id><updated>2026-11-25T00:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T16:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368--aa300b774c88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-growing-exodus-of-young-talent/a-79960368?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Conflict and uncertainty are driving more and more educated young Iranians to consider leaving the country.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
